{% extends "layouts/docs" %}

{% block content %}
	<p>These filters round numbers and format numbers and dates for readers. Formatting uses the JavaScript <code>Intl</code> API, so it handles locales, currencies and time zones without extra libraries.</p>

	<h2><code>abs</code></h2>

	<p>Returns the absolute value of a number.</p>

	{{ '{{ (-5)|abs }}'|example }}

	<p>Note the brackets. Filters bind tighter than a minus sign, so <code>-5|abs</code> means <code>-(5|abs)</code>.</p>

	<h2><code>round</code></h2>

	<p>Rounds to a number of decimal places, 0 by default. The second argument is the method: <code>"common"</code> (the default, which rounds halves away from zero), <code>"ceil"</code> or <code>"floor"</code>.</p>

	{{ '{{ 3.14159|round(2) }}
{{ 2.5|round }}
{{ 2.1|round(0, "ceil") }}'|example }}

	<h2><code>formatNumber</code></h2>

	<p>Formats a number with <code>Intl.NumberFormat</code>. Pass any of its options as named arguments, plus <code>locale</code>.</p>

	{{ '{{ 1234567.891|formatNumber }}
{{ 49.5|formatNumber(style: "currency", currency: "GBP") }}
{{ 0.256|formatNumber(style: "percent") }}
{{ 1234.5|formatNumber(locale: "de-DE", minimumFractionDigits: 2) }}'|example }}

	<h2><code>formatDate</code></h2>

	<p>Formats a date with <code>Intl.DateTimeFormat</code>. It accepts a <code>Date</code>, an ISO 8601 string or milliseconds since 1970. Pass any of its options as named arguments, plus <code>locale</code> and <code>timeZone</code>. The default style is <code>dateStyle: "medium"</code>.</p>

	{{ '{{ "2026-10-15"|formatDate }}
{{ "2026-10-15"|formatDate(dateStyle: "long", locale: "en-GB") }}
{{ "2026-10-15T14:30:00Z"|formatDate(timeStyle: "short", timeZone: "Europe/London") }}
{{ "2026-10-15"|formatDate(weekday: "long", day: "numeric", month: "long") }}'|example }}

	<p>A date and time without an offset, such as <code>2026-10-15T10:00</code>, is read as UTC.</p>

	<h2>Locale and time zone</h2>

	<p>Both filters use the render's locale and time zone unless you pass them. These default to <code>"en"</code> and <code>"UTC"</code>, so output is the same on every server. Set them for the environment or for one render. See <a href="/docs/api/create-kiln/#options">Creating an environment</a>.</p>

	<h2>Missing values</h2>

	<p><code>formatNumber</code> and <code>formatDate</code> print nothing for null. An empty field never turns into 0 or today's date.</p>

	{{ '<time>{{ post.publishedAt|formatDate }}</time>'|example(context: { post: { publishedAt: null } }) }}
{% endblock %}
